        <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;PtpConfigs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• test-grandmaster — worker2, ens4f0 + ens4f1 (2 ports, same NIC = one PHC)&lt;br&gt;• test-slave1 — worker3, ens7f0 + ens7f1 (slaveOnly 1, single ptp4l instance on both ports)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The GM needs 2 ports to feed both follower ports directly. ptp4l keeps one follower port SLAVE and the other LISTENING; if the SLAVE port loses the GM, the LISTENING port transitions to SLAVE.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The solver may also pick the mirrored solution (GM: worker3 nic3, follower: worker2 nic2)." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=4;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="770" y="100" width="310" height="380" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
