        <mxCell id="e-l1" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=none;endFill=0;dashed=1;strokeColor=#cccccc;" edge="1" parent="1" source="srv2-ens3f0" target="srv1-ens1f1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points"><mxPoint x="590" y="558" /><mxPoint x="590" y="213" /></Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;PtpConfigs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• test-wpc-tbc — worker3: ens7f0 (receiver / tbc-tr) + ens7f1 &amp; ens7f2 (transmitters / tbc-tt) + ts2phc / E810&lt;br&gt;• test-grandmaster — worker, ens1f0 (local GM on receiver LAN)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Requirements&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• T-BC: WPC NIC with ≥3 ports (1 rx + 2 tx)&lt;br&gt;• Local GM: different node, same LAN as receiver; WPC+GNSS&lt;br&gt;• EXTERNAL_GM=true → TBCExtGM (no local GM)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Not in netdevsim CI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No WPC/GNSS; CI NICs also lack a true 3-port WPC. Diagram is role placement only.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;ptpcimno lab&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;CUT cnfdf31 NIC4; GM cnfdf32 NIC6; needs L7 WPC↔WPC." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=4;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="770" y="140" width="310" height="520" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
